# Where the signature of a call on numbers, with its range rule, leaves a single integer, the walk returns that integer and builds no operation (constantWhereRowLeavesOneIntegerInNumberBuiltins()).
# Fault injection, testing=UnderstateEffects:Builtin/<name>/RangeOfResult: the signature declares the least integer of its range as its only result.
# With no operation there was no check. The program printed "least" instead of "more" and did not crash, even with testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime.
# That held for Math.abs, ceil, floor, max, min, round, sign and trunc. Now, with that switch, the shortcut is not taken: the inline code is built and checked against its signature.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime globalThis.id = (x) => x;
# RIGHT: more
# RIGHT-NEXT: more
# RIGHT-NEXT: 2
# RIGHT-NEXT: went on
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# A signature that truly leaves a single integer: the sign of a number from 1 to 4. The product is folded to 2 at compile time, and the inline code stays so that it can be checked.
# RUN(TRUE): walk f4 mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# TRUE: [[sign]]: 1 @Int32 = CallInline {{*}} inlineBuiltin=MathSign
# TRUE-NEXT: = CheckProof [[sign]] checkedType=1
# RUN(SIZE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.abs/RangeOfResult globalThis.id = (x) => x;
# SIZE: more
# SIZE-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (size)
# SIZE-NEXT: in the result of a built-in or indirect call
# SIZE-NOT: went on
# SIZE: crashed with
# RUN(LARGER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.max/RangeOfResult globalThis.id = (x) => x || 1;
# LARGER: more
# LARGER-NEXT: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (larger)
# LARGER-NEXT: in the result of a built-in or indirect call
# LARGER-NOT: went on
# LARGER: crashed with
# For an operand that has no fraction, Math.round returns the operand itself, on the strength of the type of the operand's own operation.
# With the shortcut gone, the false signature is not read at all.
# RUN(WHOLE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:Builtin/Math.round/RangeOfResult globalThis.id = (x) => x;
# WHOLE: more
# WHOLE-NEXT: more
# WHOLE-NEXT: 2
# WHOLE-NEXT: went on
# WHOLE-NEXT: exited with 0
